<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Ruto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1966">1966</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Ruto is a Kenyan politician who has been president of Kenya since 2022. He rose in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kenya-african-national-union">KANU</a> under Daniel arap Moi and served as deputy president under Uhuru Kenyatta from 2013 to 2022. He was charged at the International Criminal Court over the violence after the 2007 election, but the case was ended in 2016.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-ruto.jpg" alt="William Ruto" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Kenya · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:President_Ruto_Potrait_2022_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
